        "narrative": "<p>WAE ABUNDANCE IN VERNON LAKE WAS LOW; HOWEVER, SEVERAL WAE OVER 25 IN WERE COLLECTED, INDICATING THE LAKE HAD SOME TROPHY POTENTIAL.  THE 1985 AND 1987 YEAR CLASSES WERE RELATIVELY STRONG, BUT THE CONTRIBUTION MADE BY STOCKING IN THOSE YEARS CAN- NOT BE DETERMINED.  NATURAL REPRODUCTION OR RECRUITMENT APPEARED TO BE IRREGULAR, AS EVIDENCED BY SEVERAL MISSING YEAR CLASSES.  GROWTH WAS FAST BY COOK COUNTY STANDARDS.  SMB GILL NET CATCHES WERE ABOVE AVERAGE AND SMB GROWTH WAS AVERAGE FOR COOK COUNTY.  OF THE FEW FISH COLLECTED, THE 1988 YEAR CLASS WAS THE MOST STRONGLY REPRESENTED.  LKW APPEARED TO DOMINATE THE FISH COMMUNITY IN VERNON LAKE.  THEIR ABUNDANCE WAS VERY HIGH, WITH MOST OF THE FISH CAPTURED IN THE 13 TO 15 IN RANGE.</p>",
